cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Cross-Testbed Domain Shift in Industrial IDS: An OpenPLC to MaCySTe Reproducible Case Study"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Rifat"
    family-names: "Kinali"
    email: "info@nauticmall.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/rifatkinali/cross-testbed-industrial-ids-domain-shift"
version: "1.0.0-rc1"
date-released: "2026-08-15"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  A reproducible research artifact showing that an industrial intrusion
  detection model trained and thresholded only on an OpenPLC campaign does
  not transfer reliably to the held-out MaCySTe component-integration
  campaign used in this case study. The artifact includes derived event data,
  frozen analysis code, tests, result files, and machine-verifiable
  provenance while excluding the private GÖZCÜ EDGE product source.
keywords:
  - industrial intrusion detection
  - domain shift
  - cross-testbed evaluation
  - reproducibility
  - OpenPLC
  - MaCySTe
  - maritime cybersecurity
